---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import type { Meta } from "../lib/types";
import metaData from "../../public/data/meta.json";
import { Card, Heading, buttonVariants, cn } from "@opensourcescouting/design-system";
import { correctionHref, CORRECTION_FORM_READY } from "@lib/corrections";

const meta = metaData as unknown as Meta;
---

<Base title="About — Camp Finder">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-10">
    <Heading level={1} size={2}>About Camp Finder</Heading>

    <p class="mt-4 text-base text-foreground">
      Camp Finder is an unofficial, community-built directory of the Scouts BSA resident summer
      camps that councils run across the country. There's no good way to find a camp you don't
      already know about, so we built one.
    </p>

    <Heading level={2} size={3} className="mt-8">How it works</Heading>
    <p class="mt-3 text-base text-foreground">
      Search by location, program, and features, then follow any listing to the council's own
      page. Dates, fees, and availability change all the time, so we don't mirror them here; the
      council site is always the authority. We point you to the source. We're not trying to be it.
    </p>

    <Heading level={2} size={3} className="mt-8">Where the data comes from</Heading>
    <p class="mt-3 text-base text-foreground">
      Camp and council records come from the
      <a href={meta.source_url} class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/90" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Open Scout API</a>, an open, versioned dataset of Scouting America reference data.
      Every listing shows when its facts were last checked, and anything older than a year gets
      flagged. Confirm the details on the council's page before you register.
    </p>
    {/* Stat numerals use the DS `display` face, not `font-mono`. Base.astro no
        longer requests a mono webfont, so `font-mono` now resolves to whatever
        ui-monospace the OS supplies — the only typeface in the app the design
        system never chose. Montserrat is already loaded and is the system's
        emphasis face; these three numbers do not need tabular alignment. */}
    <ul class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-3 gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      <li>
        <Card variant="elevated" className="p-3">
          <span class="display block text-xl sm:text-2xl text-foreground">{meta.camp_count}</span> camps
        </Card>
      </li>
      <li>
        <Card variant="elevated" className="p-3">
          <span class="display block text-xl sm:text-2xl text-foreground">{meta.council_count}</span> councils
        </Card>
      </li>
      <li>
        <Card variant="elevated" className="p-3">
          <span class="display block text-xl sm:text-2xl text-foreground">{meta.states_covered.length}</span> states
        </Card>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <Heading level={2} size={3} id="corrections" className="mt-8">Suggest a correction</Heading>
    <p class="mt-3 text-base text-foreground">
      Our data is only as good as its sources. If you know a camp firsthand, because you run it,
      work it, or your unit has been there, you know it better than our scrapers do. Tell us
      what's off or missing and we'll fix it.
    </p>
    {
      CORRECTION_FORM_READY && (
        <a
          href={correctionHref(undefined, "about")}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class={cn(buttonVariants({ variant: "primary", size: "md" }), "mt-4")}
        >
          Suggest a correction →
        </a>
      )
    }
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      A real person reviews every suggestion before anything changes, so an update takes a little
      while: it lands in the
      <a href={meta.source_url} class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary/90" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Open Scout API</a> first, then this site picks it up. Prefer to file it yourself? Open an
      issue or pull request there with the camp name, what's wrong, and a link that backs it up.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
      Privacy: sharing your contact is optional, and we use it only to follow up on your
      suggestion. Your correction and any source link you provide may be recorded in the open
      dataset's provenance (credited to you only if you ask). Please don't include personal
      information about youth.
    </p>

    <Heading level={2} size={3} className="mt-8">Disclaimer</Heading>
    <p class="mt-3 text-base text-foreground">
      Camp Finder is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Scouting America
      (Boy Scouts of America). All council and camp names are the property of their
      respective owners.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
